    name: "Foundation Armor AR350 Wet Look Sealer",
    category: "Solvent-Based Acrylic Sealer",
    badge: "Best Overall",
    amazonUrl: "#",
    rating: 4.7,
    reviewCount: 14200,
    pros: [
      "Delivers the deepest, richest wet look gloss of any product we tested on pavers",
      "Non-yellowing UV-stable acrylic resins maintain clarity for 3-5 years outdoors",
      "Excellent penetration into paver pores creates strong adhesion without peeling",
      "Works on concrete pavers, brick pavers, natural stone, and exposed aggregate",
      "Breathable formula allows moisture vapor transmission to prevent whitening",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Strong solvent odor during application requires good ventilation and a respirator",
      "Requires recoating every 2-3 years on driveways with regular vehicle traffic",
    ],
    bottomLine:
      "The gold standard for wet look paver sealing. If you want a deep, glossy, color-rich finish that makes your pavers look perpetually rain-soaked, AR350 is the product professional contractors reach for first.",
    description:
      "Foundation Armor AR350 has earned its reputation as the go-to wet look paver sealer among professional hardscape installers, and our 12-month field testing confirms that reputation is well deserved. This solvent-based acrylic sealer produces the deepest, most dramatic wet look finish of any product in our test group — pavers that looked flat, dusty, and washed out were transformed into rich, glossy surfaces with colors that appeared two to three shades darker and more saturated. The key to AR350's superior performance lies in its solvent-based delivery system. The xylene carrier penetrates deeply into the pore structure of concrete and brick pavers before evaporating, depositing acrylic resins both on the surface and within the top layer of the paver material. This creates a mechanical bond that is significantly stronger than what water-based sealers achieve, which is why AR350 resists peeling and delamination far better than its water-based competitors in our durability testing. On our test installation of tumbled concrete pavers, the AR350 maintained approximately 85 percent of its original gloss intensity after 12 months of full weather exposure including two freeze-thaw cycles. The color enhancement was particularly impressive on earth-toned pavers — warm browns, tans, and terracotta shades gained tremendous depth and richness that made the hardscape look freshly installed. The non-yellowing UV-stable resin formulation is critical for outdoor paver applications where the sealed surface receives direct sunlight for hours each day. Cheaper acrylic sealers use resin blends that break down under UV radiation, turning yellow or amber within 12 to 18 months. AR350 uses premium UV-stabilized acrylic polymers that maintain their crystal-clear transparency year after year. Application is straightforward with either a pump sprayer or a three-eighths-inch nap roller. Apply two thin coats with four to six hours of dry time between coats. Coverage runs 200 to 300 square feet per gallon depending on paver porosity. At $45 to $55 per gallon, it represents strong value for a professional-grade solvent-based sealer.",
  },
  {
    id: "super-seal-30",
    name: "SuperSeal 30 High Gloss Sealer",
    category: "Solvent-Based Acrylic Sealer",
    badge: "Highest Gloss",
    amazonUrl: "#",
    rating: 4.6,
    reviewCount: 8900,
