    bottomLine:
      "The ultimate color restoration wet look sealer for aging pavers. If your once-vibrant paver patio has faded to pale ghosts of its original color, Color Boost brings it back dramatically.",
    description:
      "Techniseal Color Boost occupies a unique position in the paver sealer market as a product that was engineered from the ground up specifically for interlocking concrete pavers and natural stone. While most competing sealers are general-purpose concrete products that happen to work on pavers, Techniseal designed Color Boost with paver-specific chemistry that optimizes color enhancement, joint sand stabilization, and surface film characteristics for the unique demands of segmental pavement. The color enhancement is genuinely impressive and clearly superior to generic concrete sealers when applied to pavers. On our test installation of eight-year-old Holland-style concrete pavers that had faded significantly from years of UV exposure, the Color Boost application restored colors to approximately 90 percent of their original factory intensity. The reds became rich and warm again, the charcoal accents darkened to their original depth, and the overall paver field regained the vibrant, dimensional appearance that had slowly washed away over the years. The wet look finish falls in the satin-to-semi-gloss range, which looks particularly natural and attractive on tumbled and textured paver surfaces. The joint sand stabilization is a critical feature for paver installations. Techniseal formulated Color Boost to partially penetrate into the joint sand between pavers, creating a hardened crust that locks the sand in place and prevents erosion from rain, foot traffic, and the dreaded leaf blower that scatters joint sand across driveways and patios every fall. This is especially important when paired with Techniseal's own polymeric sand products, creating an integrated system where the sealer and joint sand work together for maximum durability. Application follows standard solvent-based procedures, but Techniseal recommends pump sprayer application rather than roller for optimal results on interlocking pavers. The sprayer delivers a more uniform, controlled application that prevents excessive sealer buildup in the beveled edges and joints between individual pavers. Apply two thin coats with six to eight hours between coats. Coverage is 100 to 200 square feet per gallon depending on paver porosity and surface texture. At $55 to $75 per gallon, Color Boost commands a premium price that reflects its paver-specific engineering and professional-grade formulation. For homeowners with aging paver installations that need both sealing and color restoration, the investment is justified by results that generic products simply cannot match.",
  },
  {
    id: "black-diamond-wet-look",
    name: "Black Diamond Stoneworks Wet Look Sealer",
